<title>UK: JG Summit plans $200 million Eurobond - dealers.</title>
<headline>JG Summit plans $200 million Eurobond - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine conglomorate JG Summit Holdings Inc plans to launch a $200 million seven-year Eurobond next week, syndicate managers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;JG Summit will issue a bond early next week,&quot; a Eurobond trader said. Spread talk was in the mid to upper-mid 100s basis points over U.S. Treasury notes, he said.</p>
<p>ING Barings was tipped as lead manager.</p>
<p>Last October ING Barings underwrote a $200 million May 2002 Eurobond for JG Summit. The deal was priced to yield 180 b.p. over U.S. Treasuries.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
</text>
